+# qos_emphasis.dem — Story 3.2 golden: the emphasis dial changes lane
+# proportions. Era-3 demand (email 4/tick res->res + streaming 2/tick
+# host->res) flows over a res->router->host backbone. At 3000ms the dial on
+# pipe 1 (router->host — draw order: 0=res-router, 1=router-host) is set to
+# express_heavy (4:2:1) and streaming is promoted to Express on that pipe
+# (per-pipe lane override); at 9000ms the dial moves to best_effort_heavy
+# (1:2:4). The T1 manifest pins the whole run; the T2 captures pin the
+# proportions VISIBLY changing (the named golden):
+#   1000ms = default balanced (no lane segments — byte-identical to 3.1's
+#            pipe render), 5000ms = express-heavy segments, 12000ms =
+#            best-effort-heavy segments.
+# fixture qos = the 3-node fixture + residentials 3,4. Node ids: 0=res,
+# 1=router, 2=host, 3=res, 4=res. Pipe ids (draw order): 0=res-router,
+# 1=router-host.
+seed 3003
+run 15000ms
+era 3
+fixture qos
+expect hash stable
+at 100ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 100ms draw 3 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 4 1 standard
+at 3000ms emphasis 1 express_heavy
+at 3000ms lane 1 streaming express
+at 9000ms emphasis 1 best_effort_heavy
+capture at 1000ms
+capture at 5000ms
+capture at 12000ms
